      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A randomized double-blind trial was carried out in 54 women to evaluate the effectiveness of ciramadol in a single (60 or 30 mg) oral dose regimen, compared with 60 mg codeine and placebo, in the treatment of post-episiotomy pain. Ciramadol gave a significantly better analgesic effect, at both 2 and 6 hours, and produced negligible side-effects. Codeine did less well than placebo in this study."},
